+### Planned target distribution and integrity
+
+Installer and packaging (#48, #50) must ship every target's runtime files:
+`target.toml`, `model.toml`, `allowlist.toml`, `sensitive.toml`, `gate-vectors.toml`
+and `prompts/`. This packaging is planned; the current target folder is not yet
+packaged. Build-time `harvest.toml` and `eval/` are not shipped.
+
+Weights are referenced by `model.toml`, not in git or the package. The planned
+manifest records download URL, size, SHA-256, base model, license, training run
+(pipeline commit and dataset hash), and quantization variants. Downloads happen
+only at install or explicit update into `$XDG_DATA_HOME/nl-shell/models/`, never
+at runtime. The installer must verify SHA-256 against `model.toml` before use.
+The REPL must refuse to load weights whose hash differs from the active target's manifest.
+These integrity checks remain requirements awaiting implementation.
+
+Personalization adapters are planned to be stored per target and base-weight hash;
+the loader must not load an adapter on different weights. This compatibility
+requirement is not implemented by the current target loader (ADR-0023).
+
